        "id": 1882530
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-18T20:24:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "How would a value of 0 or -1 help maintain compatibility? If we are never going to use it, and apps are never going to receive it, why do we need it?\n\nMaybe I have misunderstood your original comment. \nDo you mean to say that we will send different broadcasts to different apps depending upon their target API version?\ngo/android-api-guidelines#constants-callbacks-compatibility appears to be a more relevant section. However that is for callbacks, not intents.",
      "parentUuid": "aa565260_d96e63c3",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 523,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 533,
        "endChar": 57
      },
      "revId": "d992f8b7fe9dbbaf004ed589fd3948f44cee79ca",
